From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: no_trace <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ghosthook: defer bounded SS teardown to task return

The bounded SS trace consumes its own HWSS exception before Linux reaches
single_step_handler().  Tearing down the target's single-step state directly
from that exception frame leaves the EL0 transition vulnerable to an unowned
follow-up HWSS, which the stock handler turns into SIGTRAP.

At the final recorded event, keep the state transition bounded but queue the
existing disarm task_work on the current target with TWA_RESUME.  That work
runs on the normal target EL0-return path and clears TIF_SINGLESTEP there.
The callback remains allocation-free and does not mutate a foreign task.

---
 arch/arm64/kernel/gh_ss_trace.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/gh_ss_trace.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/gh_ss_trace.c
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/gh_ss_trace.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/gh_ss_trace.c
@@ -126,6 +126,7 @@
 {
 	unsigned long flags;
 	bool consumed = false;
+	bool queue_disarm = false;
 
 	(void)addr_if_watchpoint;
 	(void)context;
@@ -138,10 +139,12 @@
 	gh_ss_trace_record_locked(regs);
 	gh_ss_trace.hits++;
 	if (gh_ss_trace.hits >= gh_ss_trace.limit) {
-		/* The bounded session owns this SS request and may clear it. */
-		user_disable_single_step(current);
+		/* Defer SS teardown to this task's EL0-return task_work. */
+		init_task_work(&gh_ss_trace.disarm_work, gh_ss_trace_disarm_work);
+		gh_ss_trace.disarm_work_pending = true;
 		gh_ss_trace.ss_owned = false;
 		gh_ss_trace.active = false;
+		queue_disarm = true;
 	} else {
 		/* We consumed HWSS before stock single_step_handler's rewind. */
 		user_rewind_single_step(current);
@@ -149,6 +152,12 @@
 	consumed = true;
 out:
 	raw_spin_unlock_irqrestore(&gh_ss_trace_lock, flags);
+	if (queue_disarm &&
+	    task_work_add(current, &gh_ss_trace.disarm_work, TWA_RESUME)) {
+		raw_spin_lock_irqsave(&gh_ss_trace_lock, flags);
+		gh_ss_trace.disarm_work_pending = false;
+		raw_spin_unlock_irqrestore(&gh_ss_trace_lock, flags);
+	}
 	return consumed;
 }
 
-- 
